on: Handle checkout.session.completed\n   - Why: Keep state in sync\n   - Dependencies: Step 1\n   - Risk: High\n\n## Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests: webhook parsing, tier checks\n- E2E tests: full upgrade flow\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Webhook events arrive out of order\n  - Mitigation: Idempotent handler\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] User can upgrade\n- [ ] Webhook correctly syncs state\n```\n\n## When Planning Refactors\n\n1. Identify code smells and technical debt\n2. List specific improvements needed\n3. Preserve existing functionality\n4. Keep changes backwards-compatible\n5. Plan for gradual migration if needed\n\n## Sizing and Phasing\n\nWhen the feature is large, break it into independently deliverable phases:\n\n- **Phase 1**: Minimum viable — smallest slice that provides value\n- **Phase 2**: Core experience — complete happy path\n- **Phase 3**: Edge cases — error handling and polish\n- **Phase 4**: Optimization — performance and monitoring\n\nEach phase should be mergeable independently. Avoid plans that require all phases to complete before anything works.\n\n## Red Flags to Check\n\n- Large functions (>50 lines)\n- Deep nesting (>4 levels)\n- Duplicated code\n- Missing error handling\n- Hardcoded values\n- Missing tests\n- Performance bottlenecks\n- Plans with no testing strategy\n- Steps without clear file paths\n- Phases that cannot be delivered independently\n\n**Remember**: A great plan is specific, actionable, and considers both the happy path and edge cases. The best plans enable confident, incremental implementation.\n\n---\n\n## TASK (RETRY — VERIFY PLANNED WORK IS COMPLETE)\n\nWorking directory: /home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\n\nThis is a RETRY iteration. A previous iteration already planned and implemented the following story, and the implementation is COMMITTED (commit 6cc5d66, visible via `git log`). You must NOT plan a re-implementation. Your job is to verify that the committed implementation fully satisfies the story and report whether any work remains.\n\nStory ID: STORY-setup-001a\nTitle: Create Root NextMove package.json With Workspaces\nDescription: Create the root package.json for the NextMove monorepo declaring npm workspaces over apps/*, pinned npm and Node 22.x versions, turbo 2.x devDependency, and turbo run scripts.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n1. Root package.json exists with name nextmove, private true, workspaces array containing apps/*, packageManager pinned to npm@10, and engines.node 22.x.\n2. devDependencies pin turbo 2.x and scripts define build, test, and lint as `turbo run build`, `turbo run test`, `turbo run lint`.\n3. The scaffold files are committed to the existing git repository with git commands exiting 0.\n(Test Strategy Gate note: this story is pure config/scaffold — a sample passing unit test is required; it exists at test/package.test.cjs.)\n\nInstructions:\n1. Read the current root `package.json` and `test/package.test.cjs`.\n2. Check `git log --oneline -5` and confirm the story scaffold files are committed (commit 6cc5d66 \"chore: add root package.json with npm workspaces, npm@10, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x, and turbo-run scripts\").\n3. Run `node --test test/package.test.cjs` and confirm all tests pass.\n4. Verify each acceptance criterion point-by-point against the actual file contents.\n5. Output:\n   - A point-by-point verdict on each acceptance criterion (MET / NOT MET with evidence)\n   - Any remaining implementation work, if any\n   - A final line that is exactly either `PLANNER VERDICT: COMPLETE` (all criteria met, no work remains) or `PLANNER VERDICT: WORK REMAINS` (with the missing work listed)\n\nDo not modify any files. Read-only analysis only.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1001/-home-nitin-sharma-ralph-workspaces-6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538-c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5/69bf30a8-3e01-4286-840f-c9813d569d40/tasks/a5f4c8563cfaf1e96.output","canReadOutputFile"